# ICT FX PRO IFVG SYSTEM V6.0

- url: https://www.tradingview.com/script/jVB6yeRr-ICT-FX-PRO-IFVG-SYSTEM-V6-0/
- type: indicator
- pine_id: PUB;c73dede1cbb7458bb3f582beeab7e26f
- version: 4.0

## Description

ICT FX PRO IFVG SYSTEM V 6.0

OVERVIEW
ICT FX PRO IFVG SYSTEM is a complete ICT execution framework built around one high-probability model: the Inversion Fair Value Gap (IFVG) that forms after a liquidity sweep at a key level.

Instead of filling the chart with every gap and level, the indicator keeps your workspace clean. It brings forward only the information that matters at the moment it matters, and explains every setup through its drawings and alerts.


THE IFVG MODEL
A valid IFVG requires the full sequence of an ICT reversal:

- Liquidity is taken: price sweeps a swing high or low into a fresh extreme.
- Displacement: the move into that extreme leaves a Fair Value Gap.
- Inversion: price closes back through that gap, turning it into an IFVG.

Only clean, well-positioned gaps are accepted. Weak, small or late gaps are filtered out automatically, so what reaches your chart is a model worth your attention.

Each IFVG shows its context:
- the liquidity that was swept ($$$)
- the liquidity target it is aiming for (🎯), marked inside the IFVG once it is reached
- the higher-timeframe zone the reversal started from, when there is one


CONFLUENCE
These add confidence to a setup but are never required for it:

- CISD: shown when a Change In State of Delivery confirms the reversal.
- SMT Divergence: shown when the correlated market fails to confirm the sweep. NQ, ES and YM are compared with each other; GC is compared with Silver.


HIGHER-TIMEFRAME CONTEXT
- Up to five higher-timeframe FVG / IFVG slots, from 15m to Weekly.
- Each gap is validated on its own timeframe.
- Gaps stay in the background and act as reversal zones for the model. Enable SHOW ALL to display them on the chart.


KEY LEVELS & LIQUIDITY
- Asia, London and New York session highs and lows
- Buy-side and sell-side liquidity pools (BSL / SSL)
- Midnight, 8:30 and 9:30 opens
- Previous day, week and month high, low and close
- New Day and New Week Opening Gaps (NDOG / NWOG)

Levels are drawn compactly around current price. Overlapping levels are merged into one label.


PREMIUM & DISCOUNT
- Automatic dealing ranges with Premium, Discount and Equilibrium.
- A compact multi-timeframe bias table: Weekly, Daily, 4H and 1H.


SESSION BREAKOUT
Two predefined session ranges with breakout alerts when a candle closes outside the range.


ALERTS
Every alert states the market, the timeframe and the reason behind the setup.

- NEW IFVG: a complete model has formed.
- NEAR IFVG: price is returning to the IFVG. This is your retest alert.

Example:
🟢 NEW IFVG ← 1H IFVG + ASIA L + SMT | MNQ | 1M

Additional alerts are available for liquidity sweeps, key levels, session highs and lows, premium/discount, higher-timeframe gaps and session breakouts.


HOW TO USE
1. Focus on the Asia, London or New York session.
2. Wait for a complete IFVG model to form. Use the NEW IFVG alert to stay informed without watching the screen.
3. Do not enter on the formation. Wait for price to return to the IFVG; the NEAR IFVG alert notifies you.
4. Execute on the retest, with your stop beyond the swept high or low.
5. Manage the trade toward the marked liquidity target.
6. The setup is invalid if price closes back through the IFVG or takes the swept extreme first.

CISD and SMT strengthen a setup; use them to prioritize between models.


RECOMMENDED MARKETS
Designed and tested on CME index and metals futures:
- NQ / MNQ — Nasdaq 100
- ES / MES — S&P 500
- YM / MYM — Dow Jones
- GC / MGC — Gold

Recommended execution timeframes: 1m to 5m.


SETTINGS
All features can be switched on or off individually, and every option includes a tooltip. After changing any setting, re-create your alerts so they use the new configuration.


DISCLAIMER
This indicator is a charting and educational tool. It does not provide financial advice or guaranteed signals. Always apply proper risk management.

